```

75,000 GiB ÷ 1024 = 73.24 TiB

```

---

### Cost per TiB (ingest)

```

$4,800 ÷ 73.24 TiB ≈ $65 per TiB

```

---

### Key takeaway
> **Ingest costs us about $65 per TiB, paid once when the data arrives.**

This is the **largest cost driver** in log billing.

---

## 3. Retention Cost — Storing Logs Over Time

### What retention means
Retention is the cost of **keeping logs stored**, charged **per day**.

Dynatrace bills this as **GiB-day / TiB-day**.

